  to retrofit.

  [1mSection 4: Testing & error handling[0m

  Vitest, unit tests concentrated where the logic actually is:

  ┌────────────┬─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
  │   Target   │                                            What's tested                                            │
  ├────────────┼─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
  │ [38;5;153mmodel/[39m     │ Pure mutators, and the date predicates ([38;5;153misOverdue[39m, [38;5;153misDueToday[39m) with [38;5;153mnow[39m injected — no fake timers   │
  │            │ needed                                                                                              │
  ├────────────┼─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
  │ [38;5;153mpersist.ts[39m │ Round-trip, plus the ugly cases: malformed JSON, missing fields, wrong [38;5;153mschemaVersion[39m, quota         │
  │            │ exceeded                                                                                            │
  ├────────────┼─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
  │ [38;5;153mstore.ts[39m   │ Commands produce expected state; subscribers fire                                                   │
  └────────────┴─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘

  [38;5;153mrender[39m gets no unit tests — asserting on DOM structure at this scale tests the test, not the app. That's the gap E2E
  would cover if you add it later.

  Errors surface in one place: a dismissible banner region driven by store state. Nothing throws into a void, nothing
  blocks the app.

  ---

  That's the complete design for sub-project 1. To restate the boundary so it's explicit: [1mthis ships a working [0m
  [1msingle-user task app with due dates and no notifications.[0m Your original ask — reminders and change notifications — is
  sub-project 2, and gets its own brainstorm once these fields are real. The groundwork this lays for it is the
  [38;5;153msubscribe()[39m seam, the date predicates in [38;5;153mmodel/[39m, and [38;5;153mownerId[39m.

  If that's right, I'll write it up as a spec at [38;5;153mdocs/hyperpowers/specs/2026-09-16-task-core-design.md[39m (uncommitted) for
  you to review before we go anywhere near an implementation plan.

